\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Tell me the old, old story
\par Of unseen things above,
\par Of Jesus and His glory,
\par Of Jesus and His love.
\par Tell me the story simply,
\par As to a little child;
\par For I am weak, and weary,
\par And helpless, and defiled.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Tell me the old, old story
\par Of Jesus and His love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Tell me the story slowly,
\par That I may take it in-
\par That wonderful redemption,
\par God's remedy for sin.
\par Tell me the story often,
\par For I forget so soon;
\par The early dew of morning
\par Has passed away at noon.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Tell me the old, old story
\par Of Jesus and His love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Tell me the story softly,
\par With earnest tones and grave;
\par Remember, I'm the sinner
\par Whom Jesus came to save.
\par Tell me the story always,
\par If you would really be
\par In any time of trouble
\par A comforter to me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Tell me the old, old story
\par Of Jesus and His love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Tell me the same old story
\par When you have cause to fear
\par That this world's empty glory
\par Is costing me too dear.
\par Yes, and, when that world's glory
\par Shall dawn upon my soul,
\par Tell me the old, old story-
\par Christ Jesus makes thee whole!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Tell me the old, old story
\par Of Jesus and His love.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

